# Whether every member of an interval with 2-limb bounds is positive, and the interval is not empty
# (milestone2.md, "One enclosure interface", the row of certainly_positive()): the same on the
# leading limb of the lower bound, which has the sign of the bound (a normalized pair whose leading
# limb is zero is zero). Exact. For every precision.
kernel:        interval_positive_2
input:         xl = xl0 xl1
input:         xu = xu0 xu1
output:        mask m
requires:      interval xl xu
ensures:       certain m lt 0 x x=xl,xu exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the leading limb of the lower bound compared with 0 and +inf (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand
unused:        xl1 the leading limb of a canonical bound has its sign, and is +inf exactly when the bound is
unused:        xu0 the lower bound alone tells
unused:        xu1 the lower bound alone tells

a = lt(0, xl0)
b = lt(xl0, const inf)
m = and(a, b)
